[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 1"""
 date="2026-10-30T06:33:34Z"
 content="""
It does work for special remotes, but not for git remotes.

I think the reason for the difference is that Annex.Proxy has
proxyGitRemoteSide and proxySpecialRemoteSide. The former opens a P2P
connection to the proxied remote's git-annex-shell, and so it does not
access the remote via a Remote object like the latter does. So the fact
that the Remote has methods that have been made readonly has no effect.

So probably proxySpecialRemoteSide needs to look at annex-readonly and then
somehow limit the P2P connection to ServeReadOnly. But I don't think there
is actually any way to do that, short of modifying git-annex-shell or
somehow injecting `GIT_ANNEX_SHELL_READONLY` into its environment when
running it. So supporting it might involve consuming the P2P protocol
and filtering out writes before relaying it. Unfortunately, that would
add copying of DATA, so could be a significant slowdown.
"""]]
